@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About — Blazor Atoms</PageTitle>

<h1>About this demo</h1>

<p>
    This site is the live playground for <strong>Blazor Atoms</strong> — a family of small,
    self-contained Blazor component libraries. Each library ships as its own NuGet package with
    ~zero third-party dependencies: take one component, one library, or several, and it just
    works. No umbrella package, no global theme provider, no <code>builder.Services.Add…()</code>
    registration, no <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> tag to wire up.
</p>

<p>
    Every component is plain Blazor plus inline SVG/CSS — themeable through CSS custom
    properties, crisp at any zoom, animatable in pure CSS. JavaScript is used only where a
    browser primitive truly needs it, and always self-loads invisibly to the consumer. This app
    runs standalone <strong>Blazor WebAssembly</strong>, and every demo below runs unchanged in
    Server or Auto too.</p>

